  "result": "The gate passed `NRS_484B_110` on the first run, out of a budget of 6. It returned `OK` with all 4 witnesses.\n\n**What the rule says:**\n- **Who it covers:** any road user in the vehicle definition the node claims (`ru_aggregate` with `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **When it applies:** whenever the vehicle is moving, meaning it is not at a complete halt under the run's speed tolerance (`p.halt_speed_tolerance`). \"At any time\" means every observation is checked, so I added no time window.\n- **The duty:** the vehicle's footprint overlaps no safety zone (`∀ safety_zone z, ¬ rel_occupies(subject, z)`).\n\n**Choices:** the node left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings of my own. Its two existing narrowings (reading \"driven\" as moving, and \"safety zone\" as a marked zone region) are written from its atoms and not repeated in the rule.\n\n**Witnesses:** a safety zone 8 m long and 4 m wide, and an eastbound car:\n- **forbid:** the car drives through the zone at 8 m/s and is inside it at two observations → violated.\n- **permit:** the car drives at 8 m/s, 6 m clear of the zone → compliant.\n- **idle:** the car is at rest for the whole recording → not applicable.\n- **blind:** same as permit, but the source does not report which regions the car overlaps → unknown.\n\nI didn't find anything wrong with the node or the concept it uses. The summary is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
